  "id": "cs-user-info-bracket-stealer",
  "name": "CSUserInfoBracketStealer",
  "classification": "cystack_named",
  "attribution_confidence": "unknown",
  "description": "CyStack tracking name for an unattributed Windows\n`Information.txt` template built from `[User Info]`, `[Network]`,\n`[System]`, `[Drives]`, `[GPU]`, and `[Basic]` sections. The same\nfield grammar has been observed with the self-labels `AETHERIS`,\n`PDRstealer`, and `Banshee v1.4`, and with no surviving banner.\nThe AETHERIS-labelled observation carries the `Developer\n@sexyweekly` watermark and was distributed in an `@BRADMAX`-style\npack. These labels are retained only as per-variant panel brands.",
  "aliases": [
    "Aetheris Stealer (observed self-label)",
    "Banshee v1.4 (observed self-label)",
    "PDRstealer (observed self-label)",
    "User Info / Input ISO bracket template"
  ],
  "typical_targets": [
    "Browser saved credentials and cookies",
    "Crypto wallet extensions and clients",
    "System hardware and locale inventory"
  ],
  "detection_notes": "Primary shape is `[User Info]` plus `Input ISO:`. Stripped forms\nretain `[Basic]` plus line-anchored `User Domain:`, or\nline-anchored `Hwid:` plus `CPU Name:`. The pinned ToxSteal source\nemits the same six sections and field vocabulary, while the\nindependent IRoveroll analysis documents the same\n`Information.txt` layout and clipboard routine. Exact template\nreuse is not evidence of payload identity or common lineage.\n`AETHERIS`, `PDRstealer`, and `Banshee v1.4` are self-labels only;\nthe last does not imply a relationship to the separately\ndocumented macOS malware named Banshee.",
